n the right.","target":"eq1_fig07_fig7.png","line":202,"embedded":true},{"title":"BB vs BTN on J♠8♥5♥ — bucket view of the distribution.","target":"eq1_fig09_fig9.png","line":225,"embedded":true},{"title":"J♠8♥5♥ buckets: BTN holds 2× the best hands, ⅓ the worst.","target":"eq1_fig10_fig10.png","line":247,"embedded":true},{"title":"BTN A5s sits at the (62%, 57%) coordinate on the equity graph — better than 62% of BTN's range, 57% equity vs BB.","target":"eq1_fig11_fig11.png","line":269,"embedded":true},{"title":"River runout K♥J♦5♦ 2♣ Q♥ — BTN polarized, BB condensed.","target":"eq1_fig12_fig12.png","line":307,"embedded":true},{"title":"BTN's nut advantage on the Q♥ river: equity is 50/50 but the shape is wildly asymmetric.","target":"eq1_fig13_fig13.png","line":310,"embedded":true},{"title":"Q♥J♥8♣ A♥ board — BTN has a middling 52% range advantage, no nut advantage. Small to medium sizings only.","target":"eq1_fig14_btn_vs_bb_equity_distribution.png","line":329,"embedded":true}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
